+      <ul bare="false" empty="false" indent="3" spacing="normal" pn="section-1-3">
+        <li pn="section-1-3.1">RIPE acts as a forum for the exchange of technical information
+and the creation of expertise on IP networking.</li>
+        <li pn="section-1-3.2">The area of relevance for RIPE is Europe.</li>
+        <li pn="section-1-3.3">All parties operating wide area IP networks are encouraged to
+participate.</li>
+        <li pn="section-1-3.4">RIPE promotes and coordinates interconnection of IP networks
+within Europe and to other continents.</li>
+        <li pn="section-1-3.5">RIPE establishes agreement on common network management
+practices and the operational management of the interconnected
+networks.</li>
+        <li pn="section-1-3.6">RIPE serves as a focal point for other common activities of the
+participants related to IP networking.</li>
+        <li pn="section-1-3.7">All documents produced by RIPE will be publicly available.</li>
+        <li pn="section-1-3.8">RIPE is not a network service provider.  IP networks
+collaborating in RIPE remain under the executive authority of
+their respective organisations.</li>
+      </ul>
